WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.900
"Dahmer" tells a dark story,&nbsp;
but behind the scenes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:06.240
things allegedly got ugly in a different way.

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:10.800
When you craft a story about one of the&nbsp;
world's most depraved serial killers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:14.340
you can probably expect some&nbsp;
backlash. Netflix is getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:18.840
that backlash from several directions over&nbsp;
their latest "based-on-a-true-crime" story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:25.020
the ever-so-slightly-confusingly-titled&nbsp;
"Dahmer – Monster: The Jeffrey Dahmer Story."

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:30.660
Starring Evan Peters as the infamous Jeffrey&nbsp;
Dahmer, this streaming series looks at both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:35.400
Dahmer's childhood and his victims. The&nbsp;
details behind the killings are sordid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:39.480
and stomach-churning, which is why the&nbsp;
story of the crimes have been told and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:45.060
retold over and over again, in books,&nbsp;
movies, and now this limited series.

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:51.540
Currently holding around a 53% critic score&nbsp;
and an 84% audience score on Rotten Tomatoes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:55.800
"Dahmer" is proving to be divisive&nbsp;
with audiences. But the production&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:59.820
of the series was also a struggle for&nbsp;
some of the people involved. Here's why.

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:04.680
Despite the lukewarm critical response&nbsp;
to the show, the popularity of Netflix's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:09.840
"Dahmer" series is off the charts. Already, the&nbsp;
show has set a staggering record by being the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:16.020
most watched program in 60 countries, and&nbsp;
netting around 196.2 million viewed hours.

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:21.960
According to Variety, the show also generated&nbsp;
headlines after some viewers expressed misgivings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:27.420
with Netflix tagging the streaming show&nbsp;
with an "LGBTQ" tag. Some viewers perceived&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:32.880
this tag as being more appropriate for more&nbsp;
lighthearted, inclusive content, and not shows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:38.160
involving serial killers. The backlash was loud&nbsp;
enough that Netflix ended up removing the tag.

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:41.520
This isn't the only negative&nbsp;
headline to come "Dahmer's"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:45.300
way. Although the killer's crime spree&nbsp;
took place more than thirty years ago,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:48.780
some of Dahmer's victims have family&nbsp;
members who are very much alive.

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:54.960
Rita Isbell, who is the sister of 19-year-old&nbsp;
victim Errol Lindsay, had her statement from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.960 --> 00:02:00.720
Jeffrey Dahmer's trial recreated in Netflix's&nbsp;
show, which didn't exactly sit well with her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:05.640
In an essay published by Insider, Isbell&nbsp;
shared her thoughts about the Netflix series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:10.500
and the renewed notoriety it brought her,&nbsp;
her brother, and her brother's killer.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:15.900
After watching some of the series, she says that&nbsp;
the content bothered her – especially the moment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:20.820
where her impact statement was recreated&nbsp;
verbatim under her real name. She said,

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:25.860
"I was never contacted about the show. I&nbsp;
feel like Netflix should've asked if we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:31.170
mind or how we felt about making it. They&nbsp;
didn't ask me anything. They just did it."

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:34.680
"Whatever your name is, Satan, I'm mad."

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:39.180
Lindsey said that the recreation made her feel&nbsp;
like she was living the moment all over again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:43.320
and the fact that she and other victims'&nbsp;
families appear to have got nothing out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:45.960
of the arrangement sat poorly with her. She said,

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:50.700
"I'm not money hungry, and that's what&nbsp;
this show is about, Netflix trying to get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:55.500
paid. [...] It's sad that they're just making&nbsp;
money off of this tragedy. That's just greed."

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:59.640
On-set, not everyone was happy with&nbsp;
the "Dahmer" series either. One of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:04.020
the production assistants on Dahmer said it was&nbsp;
one of the worst sets they have ever worked on.

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:09.660
According to the LA Times, production assistant&nbsp;
Kim Alsup wrote in a now private tweet,

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:14.160
"I worked on this project and I was 1&nbsp;
of 2 Black people on the crew and they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:19.560
kept calling me her name. We both had&nbsp;
braids. She was dark skin and 5'10. I'm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:24.000
5'5. Working on this took everything&nbsp;
I had as I was treated horribly."

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:25.860
In an interview with the LA Times,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:29.400
Alsup elaborated that she hadn't&nbsp;
watched the series, saying,

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:32.940
"I just feel like it's going to bring&nbsp;
back too many memories of working on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:38.700
it. I don't want to have these PTSD types of&nbsp;
situations. The trailer itself gave me PTSD,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:43.440
which is why I ended up writing that tweet and&nbsp;
I didn't think that anybody was going to read."

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:48.420
Alsup also lamented that Dahmer was, quote,&nbsp;
"one of the worst shows that I've ever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:53.100
worked on," and alleged that there were no&nbsp;
mental health coordinators available on set.

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:58.080
A Netflix spokesperson told the LA Times&nbsp;
that all crew are provided access to free&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:02.520
health and wellness resources,&nbsp;
including therapists. Regardless,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:05.940
it seems as if controversy has&nbsp;
followed this new show at almost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:10.500
every step of the process, even in some&nbsp;
ways you wouldn't expect it to turn up.

